1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,766
This is Capybara Onsen.

2
00:00:01,766 --> 00:00:04,507
More and more of its guests are not people.

3
00:00:04,507 --> 00:00:08,332
They are AI agents, booking a soak on someone else's behalf.

4
00:00:09,032 --> 00:00:13,652
The onsen is about to ship an accessibility upgrade to its booking form.

5
00:00:13,652 --> 00:00:16,989
To a person, the new version looks exactly the same.

6
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:18,721
Not one pixel is different.

7
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:21,749
But an AI agent does not look at pixels.

8
00:00:21,749 --> 00:00:23,611
It reads the accessibility tree,

9
00:00:23,611 --> 00:00:26,986
and there the two versions could hardly be more different.

10
00:00:27,686 --> 00:00:30,555
So what does the upgrade do to the AI guests?

11
00:00:30,555 --> 00:00:32,022
We expected it to help.

12
00:00:32,022 --> 00:00:33,744
Two small pilots disagreed,

13
00:00:33,744 --> 00:00:37,570
so before the real run we registered a different prediction:

14
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:40,248
bookings will hold, and tokens will go up.

15
00:00:40,948 --> 00:00:44,281
Both versions sit behind one Flagsmith feature flag.

16
00:00:44,281 --> 00:00:49,217
A Flagsmith experiment splits the guests fifty-fifty and tracks four metrics.

17
00:00:49,917 --> 00:00:53,420
The guests are language models driving real browsers.

18
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,734
Watch this one on the classic form.

19
00:00:55,734 --> 00:00:57,783
Its preferred time is sold out,

20
00:00:57,783 --> 00:01:01,748
and the only clue in the markup is a missing pointer cursor.

21
00:01:01,748 --> 00:01:04,921
It clicks, nothing happens, and it clicks again.

22
00:01:04,921 --> 00:01:06,970
This was the worst case we saw.

23
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:11,456
On the accessible form, the same time is marked as disabled.

24
00:01:11,456 --> 00:01:15,368
The guest reads that, and goes straight to the next free slot.

25
00:01:16,068 --> 00:01:18,040
A coding agent runs the experiment,

26
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:21,025
using a skill we built on the Flagsmith command line.

27
00:01:21,025 --> 00:01:22,490
Before anything goes live,

28
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:26,883
it checks that every event arrives and that every user still gets the control.

29
00:01:26,883 --> 00:01:29,587
Then it waits for a person to approve the start.

30
00:01:30,287 --> 00:01:33,275
Three hundred guests later, this is Flagsmith's analysis.

31
00:01:33,975 --> 00:01:38,240
Correct bookings: 156 out of 156 on the classic form,

32
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,540
and 144 out of 144 on the accessible one.

33
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:43,230
No difference at all.

34
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:47,736
But tokens per guest went up by almost fourteen percent,

35
00:01:47,736 --> 00:01:50,231
and that guardrail is breached.

36
00:01:50,931 --> 00:01:51,215
Why?

37
00:01:51,215 --> 00:01:54,273
A capable agent recovers from its mistakes,

38
00:01:54,273 --> 00:01:57,260
so the bookings come out right either way.

39
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:00,887
On the classic form, 24 guests took a detour first.

40
00:02:00,887 --> 00:02:03,234
On the accessible form, none did.

41
00:02:03,234 --> 00:02:08,994
But the accessible page takes longer to read on every step, and the reading wins.

42
00:02:09,694 --> 00:02:13,330
So when the agent tries to ship, the skill refuses:

43
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:15,896
a breached guardrail needs a person.

44
00:02:15,896 --> 00:02:21,671
A person saw the result and accepted the cost, because the upgrade is for people.

45
00:02:21,671 --> 00:02:24,237
Flagsmith rolled it out to everyone.

46
00:02:24,937 --> 00:02:29,502
The skill is small on purpose: about sixteen hundred tokens of instructions,

47
00:02:29,502 --> 00:02:31,424
and one fact per line of output.

48
00:02:31,424 --> 00:02:35,148
A fresh agent ran the whole job with it in fifteen tool calls.

49
00:02:35,848 --> 00:02:40,728
And one command reruns all of it on self-hosted, open-source Flagsmith.

50
00:02:40,728 --> 00:02:43,752
We did that twice, and saw the same pattern.

51
00:02:46,452 --> 00:02:50,916
One experiment, a prediction registered in advance, and a result nobody scripted.
